            <div xml:id="d388">

                <pb facs="0384" n="268" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg268"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 123.G35/41.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-08-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 27, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On entering Hotel Miramar this evening to dine I was assaulted from behind
                    without warning or provocation by a reporter of La Prensa, who had been excluded
                    from the Legation and Department of State for lying statements and is notorious
                    for having figured in many unsavory incidents. He knocked me senseless, and
                    while in this condition he attempted to inflict further injuries. Saved from
                    serious injury by Bell. Reporter immediately arrested. Have received telephonic
                    message from President Gómez, who is in the country, and calls from Secretary of
                    State and other officials, who express regret and make spontaneous promise of
                    serious prosecution. In view of demoralizing effect of failure to press
                    prosecution of assailant of Tarler in August, 1908, and hostile attitude of part
                    of press towards United States at this time, I venture to recommend that
                    Department express interest in proper prosecution.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
